1
00:00:08,900 --> 00:00:13,340
Try lightening up on peace
and stepping away from it.

2
00:00:20,860 --> 00:00:26,860
Aiming for the day you
float on the Nakagawa,

3
00:00:27,900 --> 00:00:33,980
kick a pebble and even your shoes go flying.

4
00:00:33,980 --> 00:00:42,260
onto the head of the carpenter who
was putting someone in a chokehold.

5
00:00:42,260 --> 00:00:48,460
They laughed at me for staying a brat.

6
00:00:49,180 --> 00:00:53,540
Even if I somehow summon some energy,

7
00:00:53,540 --> 00:00:58,600
Katsushika, for it,
one yawn, nothing changes.

8
00:00:58,600 --> 00:01:02,500
The streets feel strangely gentle.

9
00:01:03,980 --> 00:01:10,520
From the pointed hat's water bottle,

10
00:01:11,180 --> 00:01:16,760
the sunset falls toward the borrowed shop.

11
00:01:20,800 --> 00:01:25,240
Tomorrow too, it ends just like this

12
00:01:25,240 --> 00:01:30,380
Katsushika Shibamata, again,
even happiness is lost.

13
00:01:30,380 --> 00:01:33,940
Because I'm a fool who finally realized it.

14
00:01:39,320 --> 00:01:41,680
The man who chases love, Kankichi Ryotsu

15
00:01:42,180 --> 00:01:44,720
People call me the hunter of love.

16
00:01:44,720 --> 00:01:49,780
Looking back, I was popular even as a child.

17
00:01:50,460 --> 00:01:51,420
But what happened?

18
00:01:51,420 --> 00:01:53,180
These women these days,

19
00:01:53,180 --> 00:01:55,440
they don't understand my charm at all.

20
00:01:56,120 --> 00:01:58,140
Whenever a romance finally comes along,

21
00:01:58,140 --> 00:01:59,523
it turns out to be a
case of mistaken identity,

22
00:01:59,573 --> 00:02:02,620
a Tarzan-like woman, or actually a man!

23
00:02:02,620 --> 00:02:04,110
What's a man to do?

24
00:02:04,160 --> 00:02:07,240
I've been the number one man people
don't want to marry for ten years running.

25
00:02:08,520 --> 00:02:11,340
Somewhere out there,

26
00:02:11,340 --> 00:02:14,100
there must surely be a woman who
understands how wonderful I am.

27
00:02:16,440 --> 00:02:18,500
Burn! Love of Erabujima

28
00:02:19,300 --> 00:02:27,260
What's this?

29
00:02:28,500 --> 00:02:30,440
I'm giving you three
days off starting today.

30
00:02:30,440 --> 00:02:33,020
You're going to Hokkaido
without saying a word.

31
00:02:33,020 --> 00:02:34,180
Hokkaido?

32
00:02:34,500 --> 00:02:37,480
It's a plane ticket for
the 9 a.m. flight tomorrow.

33
00:02:38,020 --> 00:02:39,940
Don't you dare miss it.

34
00:02:39,940 --> 00:02:41,440
Wh-, wait a minute, please wait.

35
00:02:41,440 --> 00:02:44,120
Why do I have to go to Hokkaido?

36
00:02:44,780 --> 00:02:47,060
There's an acquaintance's
daughter in Hokkaido.

37
00:02:47,660 --> 00:02:49,040
Go to a marriage meeting.

38
00:02:49,040 --> 00:02:50,540
Eeeeeeeh?

39
00:02:51,500 --> 00:02:53,260
I showed them your photo,

40
00:02:53,260 --> 00:02:55,800
and for some reason,
they really took a liking to you.

41
00:02:56,180 --> 00:02:58,480
They said they absolutely want
to meet as soon as possible.

42
00:02:58,940 --> 00:03:01,060
So I figured we should do it
before they change their minds.

43
00:03:01,060 --> 00:03:03,440
I have an important meeting tomorrow,
so I can't go.

44
00:03:03,440 --> 00:03:05,560
Ryotsu, you go on ahead.

45
00:03:05,560 --> 00:03:09,220
Understood!
Ryotsu and Kankichi, we're off to Hokkaido!

46
00:03:10,260 --> 00:03:12,700
Airline tickets should be refundable.

47
00:03:12,700 --> 00:03:16,140
If I get three days off and
the refund money comes through,

48
00:03:18,320 --> 00:03:19,900
W-what is it, Chief?

49
00:03:19,900 --> 00:03:23,060
You're not planning to get a refund on that ticket,
are you?

50
00:03:23,060 --> 00:03:25,120
No, no, come on, Chief.

51
00:03:27,260 --> 00:03:28,280
Listen, Ryotsu.

52
00:03:28,980 --> 00:03:31,160
Once the meeting is over,
go to the arranged meeting.

53
00:03:31,160 --> 00:03:32,500
I'll rush over after you.

54
00:03:34,660 --> 00:03:36,760
If you don't go to Hokkaido,

55
00:03:36,760 --> 00:03:38,680
you know what will happen.

56
00:03:38,680 --> 00:03:40,700
That's just a threat, isn't it?

57
00:03:40,700 --> 00:03:42,780
Then I'm not going to any arranged meeting.

58
00:03:42,780 --> 00:03:43,860
You idiot.

59
00:03:44,400 --> 00:03:46,900
At your age,
with no savings and no redeeming qualities,

60
00:03:46,900 --> 00:03:49,120
the other party took a
liking to a guy like you.

61
00:03:49,120 --> 00:03:51,340
They even sent you a round-trip ticket!

62
00:03:51,780 --> 00:03:53,460
A miracle like this will never happen again.

63
00:03:53,460 --> 00:03:54,640
Fine, I get it.

64
00:03:54,640 --> 00:03:56,220
If it's just a quick meeting,

65
00:03:56,800 --> 00:04:00,260
that's fine. She's a woman
you'll like at first sight, too.

66
00:04:00,820 --> 00:04:03,500
So, in terms of celebrities,
what kind of woman is she?

67
00:04:04,520 --> 00:04:05,951
Y-yeah, that's right.

68
00:04:06,001 --> 00:04:08,540
Her style is Norika Fujiwara.

69
00:04:08,860 --> 00:04:10,620
Whoa! The one from Nice Birdie?

70
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:13,140
Her hairstyle is Izumi Inamori.

71
00:04:13,180 --> 00:04:14,600
That's amazing!

72
00:04:14,980 --> 00:04:15,660
That's insane.

73
00:04:16,120 --> 00:04:19,120
No, wait a second.
What about her face, the kanji one?

74
00:04:19,360 --> 00:04:22,583
Her face It's hard to compare,

75
00:04:22,633 --> 00:04:23,840
but if I had to say.

76
00:04:24,020 --> 00:04:24,740
If you had to say?

77
00:04:24,740 --> 00:04:28,660
She's like Kento Shimura and Hanako
Yamada mixed together and split in two.

78
00:04:40,320 --> 00:04:43,100
Kento Shimura and Hanako
Yamada showed up in my dreams

79
00:04:43,100 --> 00:04:44,760
and I couldn't sleep a wink last night.

80
00:04:45,780 --> 00:04:48,420
And this morning,
I thought Nakagawa had come to pick me up,

81
00:04:48,420 --> 00:04:50,280
but he went and strapped me to my seat!

82
00:04:50,660 --> 00:04:53,680
The chief and Nakagawa
don't trust anyone at all.

83
00:04:55,960 --> 00:04:57,280
Where do we board?

84
00:04:59,020 --> 00:05:00,720
Idiot! Watch where you're going!

85
00:05:01,320 --> 00:05:02,500
S-sorry.

86
00:05:03,160 --> 00:05:04,980
I feel like I've seen this somewhere.

87
00:05:19,060 --> 00:05:19,380
What is it?

88
00:05:20,380 --> 00:05:21,640
It's pretty warm, isn't it.

89
00:05:21,640 --> 00:05:24,380
I thought it'd be colder this time of year.

90
00:05:24,380 --> 00:05:25,260
Mr. Ryotsu.

91
00:05:26,220 --> 00:05:27,860
What do you want from me?

92
00:05:27,860 --> 00:05:28,720
Actually,

93
00:05:30,360 --> 00:05:32,800
The airline tickets got swapped?

94
00:05:32,800 --> 00:05:36,280
It was when you bumped into manga artist
Ms. Akimoto in the lobby at Haneda.

95
00:05:36,800 --> 00:05:37,480
At Haneda?

96
00:05:43,220 --> 00:05:44,600
That time.

97
00:05:45,360 --> 00:05:47,900
So this isn't Hokkaido?

98
00:05:48,300 --> 00:05:49,240
It's Kagoshima.

99
00:05:49,240 --> 00:05:50,980
Kagoshima?!

100
00:05:50,980 --> 00:05:54,560
In any case, please take the
return flight back to Haneda.

101
00:05:54,560 --> 00:05:56,000
No way.

102
00:05:56,000 --> 00:05:58,600
I took three days of paid leave for this.

103
00:05:58,600 --> 00:06:01,560
If I go back to Haneda now
and then head to Hokkaido,

104
00:06:01,560 --> 00:06:03,980
a whole day of my paid leave will be wasted,
you know!

105
00:06:03,980 --> 00:06:05,700
Even if you say that...

106
00:06:07,480 --> 00:06:10,360
I'll settle things with that manga artist,
Akimoto or whatever his name is.

107
00:06:11,040 --> 00:06:12,780
He's here, please go right in.

108
00:06:12,780 --> 00:06:15,640
So you're Akimoto?

109
00:06:16,520 --> 00:06:21,000
Yes, I have to go to Okinoerabu Island for an interview,
so please come back quickly.

110
00:06:21,640 --> 00:06:22,840
Okinoerabu Island.

111
00:06:23,340 --> 00:06:26,200
It's an island between
Amami Oshima and Okinawa.

112
00:06:26,200 --> 00:06:29,920
The locals should be waiting for me.

113
00:06:29,920 --> 00:06:33,200
Then I'll go there in your
place and do the interview.

114
00:06:33,200 --> 00:06:36,720
So you go to Sapporo in my
place for the arranged meeting.

115
00:06:37,480 --> 00:06:40,440
That's absurd!
I'm a married man with a family!

116
00:06:40,580 --> 00:06:43,000
Shut up! I've decided, so do as you're told!

117
00:06:43,240 --> 00:06:46,540
Well then, it's settled.
We're off to Okinoerabu Island!

118
00:06:46,820 --> 00:06:47,860
R-really?

119
00:06:48,100 --> 00:06:51,160
Yes. Take me to the plane
for Okinoerabu Island!

120
00:06:51,720 --> 00:06:52,260
Haah...

121
00:07:05,080 --> 00:07:06,020
Akimoto-sensei

122
00:07:09,260 --> 00:07:11,500
Even for the tropics, it's hot, isn't it?

123
00:07:13,100 --> 00:07:15,200
There's a welcoming party waiting for us.

124
00:07:15,860 --> 00:07:17,080
Hello, hello.

125
00:07:21,600 --> 00:07:22,400
Chief Ohara.

126
00:07:24,280 --> 00:07:25,540
What's wrong, Nakagawa?

127
00:07:26,520 --> 00:07:28,080
Just now, we got a call at the police box.

128
00:07:28,080 --> 00:07:30,940
It was from the father of
Ryo-chan's arranged-meeting partner.

129
00:07:30,940 --> 00:07:34,220
Apparently he wasn't on the
plane he was scheduled to take.

130
00:07:34,720 --> 00:07:35,320
What?

131
00:07:35,320 --> 00:07:38,260
Ryotsu definitely headed to Haneda this morning,
didn't he?

132
00:07:38,820 --> 00:07:40,560
Yes, I drove him there myself.

133
00:07:41,080 --> 00:07:42,160
There's no mistake.

134
00:07:42,160 --> 00:07:44,220
If he didn't oversleep...

135
00:07:44,220 --> 00:07:47,180
Hey, where is that idiot?

136
00:08:01,760 --> 00:08:03,818
Because he's a famous manga artist,

137
00:08:03,868 --> 00:08:07,760
I expected a more difficult person,
but he's quite friendly.

138
00:08:09,300 --> 00:08:10,300
Chief, just a moment.

139
00:08:10,860 --> 00:08:11,300
What?

140
00:08:13,420 --> 00:08:15,520
Stop, stop!

141
00:08:15,520 --> 00:08:17,040
What's the matter, Chief?

142
00:08:17,040 --> 00:08:18,980
Who are you?

143
00:08:18,980 --> 00:08:20,040
No.

144
00:08:20,040 --> 00:08:23,860
Who else would it be?
Osamu Akimoto, obviously.

145
00:08:23,860 --> 00:08:25,880
Mr. Akimoto is this way.

146
00:08:28,180 --> 00:08:29,240
You...

147
00:08:29,240 --> 00:08:31,080
That's terrible!

148
00:08:31,080 --> 00:08:32,680
Impersonating me, of all things!

149
00:08:32,680 --> 00:08:34,600
I thought you'd gone to Sapporo!

150
00:08:34,600 --> 00:08:38,120
Why do I have to take your
place at the arranged meeting?

151
00:08:38,120 --> 00:08:39,040
Listen, you...

152
00:08:40,760 --> 00:08:42,180
Wait, wait, wait, hold on!

153
00:08:42,180 --> 00:08:44,020
I don't want to!

154
00:08:48,500 --> 00:08:49,420
Good grief!

155
00:09:05,800 --> 00:09:21,520
Uuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuu...

156
00:09:21,520 --> 00:09:22,080
I'm going home.

157
00:09:23,500 --> 00:09:23,900
What?

158
00:09:25,280 --> 00:09:27,040
Why is it raining in the desert?

159
00:09:30,340 --> 00:09:31,140
Hey!

160
00:09:32,220 --> 00:09:34,100
You idiot! What the hell are you doing?

161
00:09:34,620 --> 00:09:35,280
You bastard!

162
00:09:35,620 --> 00:09:36,600
I'm sorry!

163
00:09:38,460 --> 00:09:41,260
I didn't know you were there!

164
00:09:41,280 --> 00:09:43,280
Shut up!
Now I've gone and swallowed it, you bastard!

165
00:09:43,420 --> 00:09:44,860
What's wrong, Hiroshi?

166
00:09:53,860 --> 00:09:55,120
R-Ritsuo-san...

167
00:10:08,480 --> 00:10:10,380
So you were a schoolteacher?

168
00:10:10,380 --> 00:10:14,480
Well, it's a school, but it's a tiny one
on the island next to the one you chose.

169
00:10:14,480 --> 00:10:18,020
From first grade through sixth,
there are only twelve students.

170
00:10:18,020 --> 00:10:19,700
Only twelve?

171
00:10:23,640 --> 00:10:25,440
In my class there were fifty!

172
00:10:26,260 --> 00:10:27,600
Ryotsu-san, is that all right?

173
00:10:27,860 --> 00:10:29,140
Even though we've only just met,

174
00:10:29,140 --> 00:10:30,880
and you carried my luggage for me.

175
00:10:31,460 --> 00:10:33,700
I was just napping anyway,
since I've got nothing to do.

176
00:10:33,700 --> 00:10:34,680
Reiko-sensei.

177
00:10:34,680 --> 00:10:37,420
This old man just tried to hit me.

178
00:10:37,420 --> 00:10:40,000
Hey, what are you talking about, little boy?

179
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:41,920
But in nature like this,

180
00:10:41,920 --> 00:10:43,840
it must be nice to be
able to educate children.

181
00:10:43,840 --> 00:10:44,840
Is that so?

182
00:10:44,840 --> 00:10:46,420
It's wonderful.

183
00:10:46,420 --> 00:10:49,320
Kids from Tokyo are so cheeky,
they're hopeless.

184
00:10:49,320 --> 00:10:51,040
Island kids are cute.

185
00:11:07,220 --> 00:11:09,380
Fifteen minutes by boat from Erabu Island

186
00:11:09,380 --> 00:11:10,740
That's pretty close, isn't it?

187
00:11:11,260 --> 00:11:13,680
But there are only three flights a day.

188
00:11:13,680 --> 00:11:15,880
The evening return flight is the last one.

189
00:11:17,200 --> 00:11:19,340
This is the elementary school where I teach.

190
00:11:19,340 --> 00:11:21,220
It's really a small school, isn't it.

191
00:11:22,060 --> 00:11:24,100
Yuriko-sensei is back.

192
00:11:24,100 --> 00:11:25,220
Yuriko-sensei!

193
00:11:25,220 --> 00:11:27,520
I'm back. Were you all good?

194
00:11:29,580 --> 00:11:31,500
Yuriko-sensei, who's this?

195
00:11:31,880 --> 00:11:32,800
He looks like a gorilla.

196
00:11:33,400 --> 00:11:35,260
That's rude,
even though it's our first meeting.

197
00:11:35,660 --> 00:11:39,360
He brought marble and coral for
everyone's teaching materials.

198
00:11:39,360 --> 00:11:41,660
This is Ryotsu-san. Let's say hello.

199
00:11:41,660 --> 00:11:42,280
Hello.

200
00:11:43,020 --> 00:11:43,380
What do you think?

201
00:11:44,400 --> 00:11:47,780
As expected of Yuriko-sensei's students,
they're so polite.

202
00:11:48,320 --> 00:11:48,680
Thank you very much.

203
00:11:48,680 --> 00:11:51,915
Thank you.
While I'm asking for favors, I'm sorry,

204
00:11:51,965 --> 00:11:53,960
could you carry that to
the science room for me?

205
00:11:54,260 --> 00:11:55,380
Yes, yes, understood.

206
00:11:55,740 --> 00:11:58,580
Well then, Shinji,
Hiromi, I'm counting on you.

207
00:11:58,780 --> 00:11:59,140
Yes.

208
00:12:00,880 --> 00:12:02,180
This is the science room.

209
00:12:06,220 --> 00:12:07,140
No good.

210
00:12:07,700 --> 00:12:08,580
Oh dear, what a problem.

211
00:12:08,780 --> 00:12:10,160
What's this, is it stuck?

212
00:12:12,320 --> 00:12:15,620
This door is crooked. It has to be fixed.

213
00:12:18,180 --> 00:12:19,780
Hey, bring me a nail and a hammer.

214
00:12:19,920 --> 00:12:20,200
Yes.

215
00:12:26,400 --> 00:12:27,960
You don't have to do that.

216
00:12:28,820 --> 00:12:32,100
Don't worry about it. I'm great at this.
Something like this is an easy fix.

217
00:12:32,620 --> 00:12:34,680
This school building seems
to be falling apart all over.

218
00:12:34,960 --> 00:12:38,460
I'll fix everything while I'm at it,
so you go and do your own work.

219
00:12:38,460 --> 00:12:40,418
Are you sure? Thank you so much.

220
00:12:40,468 --> 00:12:42,940
Then I'll be in the staff room.

221
00:12:46,460 --> 00:12:48,760
Hey, Yuriko-sensei, are you still single?

222
00:12:48,880 --> 00:12:49,140
Mm-hm.

223
00:12:49,900 --> 00:12:53,700
I see. Hehehe. My luck is finally turning.

224
00:12:54,040 --> 00:12:55,340
What did you put on this? It's hot!

225
00:12:55,520 --> 00:12:59,228
Y-you idiot! Wasn't it
"no chicken"? Hold the chicken!

226
00:12:59,278 --> 00:13:01,240
No, no, bring me some water!

227
00:13:18,180 --> 00:13:19,560
Good, this is perfect now.

228
00:13:20,260 --> 00:13:21,940
Wow, that's spot on!

229
00:13:23,040 --> 00:13:25,260
This is a piece of cake for me.

230
00:13:25,260 --> 00:13:27,640
I really don't know how to thank you.

231
00:13:27,640 --> 00:13:29,000
No need to thank me.

232
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:33,320
Oh no, the last flight to
Erabu Island has already left.

233
00:13:34,140 --> 00:13:36,960
Don't worry,
I'll just stay at an inn or a guesthouse.

234
00:13:36,960 --> 00:13:40,680
The thing is,
there are no such facilities on this island.

235
00:13:41,600 --> 00:13:43,400
What a remote place this is!

236
00:13:43,960 --> 00:13:47,140
If you don't mind,
would you like to come to my house?

237
00:13:48,000 --> 00:13:48,900
It's a small place, but...

238
00:13:48,900 --> 00:13:49,960
No, not at all.

239
00:13:49,960 --> 00:13:52,960
I can't go to the home of
a single woman living alone!

240
00:13:52,960 --> 00:13:55,600
I'll be fine sleeping in
the school's science room.

241
00:13:55,600 --> 00:13:57,440
As a thank you for
repairing the school building,

242
00:13:57,440 --> 00:13:59,360
please let me treat you to dinner.

243
00:13:59,860 --> 00:14:01,000
What? Dinner?

244
00:14:02,140 --> 00:14:03,380
Is this about me?

245
00:14:03,940 --> 00:14:05,600
Well, but...

246
00:14:05,600 --> 00:14:07,560
Aww, this is bad.

247
00:14:07,560 --> 00:14:08,820
Darn it.

248
00:14:08,820 --> 00:14:10,600
Come on.

249
00:14:11,080 --> 00:14:12,820
You're secretly happy,
but you're just embarrassed.

250
00:14:12,820 --> 00:14:13,680
Shut up!

251
00:14:14,280 --> 00:14:15,740
Don't tease a grown man!

252
00:14:16,380 --> 00:14:17,240
Stop right there!

253
00:14:17,600 --> 00:14:18,760
As if I'd stop!

254
00:14:19,040 --> 00:14:19,620
Stop right there!

255
00:14:27,520 --> 00:14:30,680
I hear you repaired all
the bookcases at Bunko.

256
00:14:30,680 --> 00:14:32,220
That's right, auntie.

257
00:14:32,220 --> 00:14:34,460
Ryo-chan is really handy, you know.

258
00:14:34,460 --> 00:14:36,060
It's nothing special.

259
00:14:37,420 --> 00:14:41,840
I never expected you'd be living
alone with the gym lady from Bunko.

260
00:14:42,280 --> 00:14:44,080
Your story is a little too good to be true.

261
00:14:46,320 --> 00:14:48,020
It's fine either way.

262
00:14:48,020 --> 00:14:51,160
Anyway,
it's just you and auntie at Bunko, then?

263
00:14:51,620 --> 00:14:54,180
There used to be five of us, including me.

264
00:14:54,700 --> 00:14:57,080
Now it's only the two of us.

265
00:14:57,520 --> 00:15:01,020
A new teacher is supposed to be
coming from Kagoshima, though.

266
00:15:01,560 --> 00:15:02,500
Not bad.

267
00:15:03,480 --> 00:15:04,560
That must be tough.

268
00:15:04,560 --> 00:15:06,880
Running that Bunko with just two people,

269
00:15:07,440 --> 00:15:08,840
mm-hmm, mm-hmm.

270
00:15:09,820 --> 00:15:12,100
Alright,
I'll start helping you from tomorrow.

271
00:15:13,360 --> 00:15:15,780
Some of the chairs in the
classroom are broken too,

272
00:15:16,120 --> 00:15:18,540
and it'd be good to repaint
the school building if possible.

273
00:15:18,540 --> 00:15:20,960
Besides, I can't teach academics,

274
00:15:20,960 --> 00:15:23,060
but I can teach PE.

275
00:15:23,780 --> 00:15:26,580
But Ryo-san, your real job is
being a police officer, right?

276
00:15:26,580 --> 00:15:27,420
Is that really alright?

277
00:15:27,420 --> 00:15:31,580
Sure, it's fine. I'm always being bullied
by a boss who just complains all the time,

278
00:15:32,060 --> 00:15:36,180
so I've been wanting to relax
in nature once in a while.

279
00:15:36,800 --> 00:15:39,200
Really? Then let's ask for your help,
Teacher Yuriko.

280
00:15:39,760 --> 00:15:40,040
But...

281
00:15:40,040 --> 00:15:40,480
But...

282
00:15:40,480 --> 00:15:41,703
What's the harm?

283
00:15:41,753 --> 00:15:44,620
Ryo-chan,
you even look like my ex-boyfriend.

284
00:15:44,760 --> 00:15:46,860
A new romance is blooming, so...

285
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:47,720
Auntie!

286
00:15:51,720 --> 00:15:53,540
Yes, yes, thanks for the meal.

287
00:15:53,900 --> 00:15:57,540
I have some errands early tomorrow morning,
so I'm going to turn in early.

288
00:15:57,780 --> 00:15:59,740
Well then, Ryo-chan,
I'm counting on you starting tomorrow.

289
00:15:59,960 --> 00:16:00,700
Right, right.

290
00:16:04,320 --> 00:16:05,600
You must be tired from today, right?

291
00:16:06,440 --> 00:16:08,620
There's a futon laid out in the next room,

292
00:16:08,620 --> 00:16:10,660
so please go ahead and get some rest.

293
00:16:11,400 --> 00:16:12,120
Ah.

294
00:16:14,400 --> 00:16:17,320
Teacher Yuriko, are you from this island?

295
00:16:17,720 --> 00:16:19,280
No, I'm from Nagasaki.

296
00:16:19,280 --> 00:16:21,240
Why did you come to this island?

297
00:16:22,800 --> 00:16:24,420
It's because I love children.

298
00:16:25,040 --> 00:16:27,540
Well, there must be elementary
schools in Nagasaki too, right?

299
00:16:27,540 --> 00:16:29,800
But why come to such a remote island?

300
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:33,000
I had some unpleasant
things happen in Nagasaki.

301
00:16:34,280 --> 00:16:35,680
It's about my ex-boyfriend.

302
00:16:36,200 --> 00:16:36,600
Yes.

303
00:16:37,500 --> 00:16:39,120
He was nothing like Ryo-san,

304
00:16:39,120 --> 00:16:40,800
he was so indecisive, I suppose.

305
00:16:41,340 --> 00:16:43,240
Not very manly, I guess.

306
00:16:43,780 --> 00:16:45,600
After all, men should be manly,

307
00:16:45,600 --> 00:16:46,740
and once they've made a decision,

308
00:16:46,740 --> 00:16:48,680
they should see it through no matter what.

309
00:16:49,380 --> 00:16:49,780
That's true.

310
00:16:50,840 --> 00:16:53,060
I'm going to make the test questions now,

311
00:16:53,060 --> 00:16:54,740
so please go ahead and rest first.

312
00:16:54,740 --> 00:16:55,520
I see.

313
00:16:55,960 --> 00:16:57,260
Well then, good night.

314
00:17:08,900 --> 00:17:09,337
Damn.

315
00:17:09,387 --> 00:17:12,960
Knowing Yuriko-sensei is right next door,
I can't get to sleep.

316
00:17:23,160 --> 00:17:24,680
She's quite a woman, isn't she?

317
00:17:25,660 --> 00:17:27,380
If only I could marry her...

318
00:17:35,640 --> 00:17:38,780
But with Yuriko-sensei, you'd expect a
truly traditional Japanese wife, right?

319
00:17:39,520 --> 00:17:44,800
I'd want more than one kid,
enough for a whole baseball team.

320
00:17:49,480 --> 00:17:50,600
What's wrong?

321
00:17:52,060 --> 00:17:54,680
No, I just had a creepy dream.

322
00:17:58,300 --> 00:18:01,280
I hope our kids look like Yuriko-sensei,
after all.

323
00:18:03,560 --> 00:18:04,640
Okinoerabu Island?

324
00:18:05,520 --> 00:18:07,240
Why are you on a place like that?

325
00:18:07,240 --> 00:18:09,460
It's a long story, so I'll leave it at that.

326
00:18:09,460 --> 00:18:11,840
You idiot! The boss is furious!

327
00:18:11,840 --> 00:18:14,220
How dare you drag my name
through the mud like this!

328
00:18:14,220 --> 00:18:17,260
Never mind that, I might be getting married.

329
00:18:17,260 --> 00:18:18,300
W-what?

330
00:18:18,500 --> 00:18:21,160
I've finally met my ideal woman.

331
00:18:21,160 --> 00:18:21,600
Really?

332
00:18:21,600 --> 00:18:23,440
Well, anyway, that's how it is.

333
00:18:24,680 --> 00:18:28,780
Hey, what's that idiot done now?

334
00:18:29,940 --> 00:18:38,340
That guy said he might get married because his ideal woman showed up.
Well, everyone, I have some very good news today.

335
00:18:38,340 --> 00:18:44,360
Yesterday he fixed the school tower, and from
today Akimoto will be helping the teacher.

336
00:18:46,860 --> 00:18:50,220
Everyone, nice to meet you, peace peace.

337
00:18:51,160 --> 00:18:54,640
Ryotsu-san, the upper grades' PE class is yours.
Is that all right?

338
00:18:54,640 --> 00:18:56,320
Leave it to me.

339
00:18:56,850 --> 00:18:58,760
Come on, get outside quickly.

340
00:18:58,760 --> 00:19:00,580
But you need to change first.

341
00:19:00,580 --> 00:19:04,480
Come on, run!
That's 100 laps around the grounds!

342
00:19:05,960 --> 00:19:09,020
It really makes a difference having a man around,
doesn't it, Yuriko-sensei?

343
00:19:09,020 --> 00:19:11,060
It really is. What a relief.

344
00:19:20,460 --> 00:19:22,220
Okay, I'm handing back the tests!

345
00:19:23,100 --> 00:19:23,740
Ichiro.

346
00:19:24,280 --> 00:19:25,620
Yeah, you worked hard.

347
00:19:27,540 --> 00:19:28,040
Hirose.

348
00:19:28,040 --> 00:19:29,620
Wow, this is terrible.

349
00:19:33,080 --> 00:19:35,900
Everyone, I'll warn you now,

350
00:19:36,320 --> 00:19:40,120
there are some of you who think
you can get by without studying,

351
00:19:43,880 --> 00:19:44,980
that's right.

352
00:19:44,980 --> 00:19:47,960
Things do work out somehow,
which is what makes life interesting.

353
00:19:48,320 --> 00:19:49,880
What's important in life is this:

354
00:19:49,880 --> 00:19:52,720
once you've decided something,
you see it through no matter what.

355
00:19:52,720 --> 00:19:54,440
That's my policy.

356
00:19:54,920 --> 00:19:57,740
So that's all for today's lesson.

357
00:19:59,220 --> 00:20:00,260
Pyokko-sensei

358
00:20:00,800 --> 00:20:01,600
Yuriko-sensei

359
00:20:01,960 --> 00:20:04,640
You've really gotten used to the children,
haven't you?

360
00:20:04,640 --> 00:20:06,380
You were listening?

361
00:20:06,380 --> 00:20:08,752
Hahaha, I love children too,
so

362
00:20:08,802 --> 00:20:10,460
I got carried away with my speech.

363
00:20:10,740 --> 00:20:12,960
How long will you stay on this island?

364
00:20:13,200 --> 00:20:16,180
H-how long?
If you'd like, I'll stay forever.

365
00:20:16,500 --> 00:20:18,880
I'd even quit being a police
officer to become a teacher.

366
00:20:19,080 --> 00:20:20,700
Good.

367
00:20:22,120 --> 00:20:22,840
Was that okay?

368
00:20:27,060 --> 00:20:27,880
Yuriko-sensei.

369
00:20:28,640 --> 00:20:34,360
T-this must be Yuriko-sensei's greatest confession,
from a bashful maiden!

370
00:20:35,700 --> 00:20:37,900
Yuriko-sensei, you've got an express letter.

371
00:20:37,900 --> 00:20:38,600
Express letter?

372
00:20:38,940 --> 00:20:41,680
Yuriko-sensei, you want to be
with me forever too, don't you?

373
00:20:41,680 --> 00:20:43,520
Alright, I'll confess.

374
00:20:43,520 --> 00:20:46,380
I love you. Please marry me.

375
00:20:47,520 --> 00:20:51,000
Stop it, Ryo-san. I'm over fifty!

376
00:20:51,880 --> 00:20:53,900
Well, if you're serious,
you could think about it.

377
00:20:53,900 --> 00:20:54,780
As for Yuriko-sensei...

378
00:20:59,560 --> 00:21:00,440
Teacher Yuriko

379
00:21:02,860 --> 00:21:03,880
What's wrong?

380
00:21:04,440 --> 00:21:05,900
You seem to have been crying,

381
00:21:11,980 --> 00:21:12,860
What? What?

382
00:21:13,480 --> 00:21:15,400
it's because I couldn't make up my mind.

383
00:21:15,400 --> 00:21:18,320
I'm sorry I made you sad.

384
00:21:18,320 --> 00:21:21,900
I've left home and am now in Kagoshima City.

385
00:21:22,740 --> 00:21:25,820
My parents won't accept our marriage,

386
00:21:25,820 --> 00:21:27,380
so I left home yesterday.

387
00:21:27,380 --> 00:21:29,680
I want to see you right away.

388
00:21:29,680 --> 00:21:31,260
And we'll talk it through.

389
00:21:35,800 --> 00:21:37,760
Were those tears of joy?

390
00:21:44,660 --> 00:21:46,580
Are you going back to Tokyo now?

391
00:21:47,120 --> 00:21:49,800
But you told me you'd stay here forever.

392
00:21:49,800 --> 00:21:53,640
Teaching is fun, but I still love
being a police officer the most.

393
00:21:53,640 --> 00:21:56,580
My colleagues at the police box must be worried about me,
I think.

394
00:21:56,580 --> 00:22:01,080
Yuriko-sensei, a typhoon is approaching,
so the boat has been cancelled.

395
00:22:01,080 --> 00:22:02,960
After all, we'd better get ready today.

396
00:22:04,360 --> 00:22:06,980
Once you've said something,
you have to follow through no matter what.

397
00:22:06,980 --> 00:22:09,400
Because that's what
I've taught the children.

398
00:22:12,740 --> 00:22:13,440
Alright!

399
00:22:13,440 --> 00:22:15,900
Are you seriously going to
swim all the way to Kagoshima?

400
00:22:15,900 --> 00:22:17,460
I'm confident in my stamina.

401
00:22:17,460 --> 00:22:19,640
If I swim for 20 hours, I'll reach Satozaki.

402
00:22:19,640 --> 00:22:22,160
From Kagoshima, we can take the
train back to Tokyo, you know.

403
00:22:22,160 --> 00:22:23,660
But that's too dangerous.

404
00:22:23,660 --> 00:22:26,320
In this storm,
we don't know where we'll end up.

405
00:22:26,320 --> 00:22:26,900
It's fine.

406
00:22:28,140 --> 00:22:29,600
Anyway, Yuriko-sensei,

407
00:22:29,600 --> 00:22:31,500
making the children happy is good,

408
00:22:31,500 --> 00:22:34,260
but you should cherish
your own happiness too.

409
00:22:34,740 --> 00:22:35,720
Ryo-san,

410
00:22:36,520 --> 00:22:38,840
did you happen to read that letter?

411
00:22:38,840 --> 00:22:40,540
Sorry, I went and read it.

412
00:22:40,540 --> 00:22:43,540
Ryo-san, I, I...

413
00:22:43,540 --> 00:22:43,800
I...

414
00:22:58,140 --> 00:22:59,060
You kids!

415
00:22:59,280 --> 00:23:01,580
Listen properly to what Yuriko-sensei says!

416
00:23:01,820 --> 00:23:02,480
Understand?

417
00:23:03,360 --> 00:23:03,680
Yeah.

418
00:23:05,480 --> 00:23:06,280
Farewell!

419
00:23:16,480 --> 00:23:20,260
Thanks to Ryotsu-san,
I was able to get back together with him.

420
00:23:20,740 --> 00:23:24,660
He's coming here too, and he'll
teach at the branch school with me.

421
00:23:24,660 --> 00:23:25,840
Thank you so much.

422
00:23:26,920 --> 00:23:31,160
I sincerely wish you happiness.

423
00:23:31,160 --> 00:23:32,500
From Yuriko

424
00:23:34,340 --> 00:23:36,280
Looks like you got dumped, senpai.

425
00:23:37,020 --> 00:23:39,820
But where on earth did he go?

426
00:23:40,360 --> 00:23:41,200
That idiot.

427
00:23:46,480 --> 00:23:49,180
He swam through a typhoon without food or water,
you know.

428
00:23:49,180 --> 00:23:50,520
Why, why?

429
00:23:50,520 --> 00:23:52,340
He went to Hong Kong.

430
00:23:54,420 --> 00:23:56,820
I'm never falling in love again.

431
00:23:57,340 --> 00:23:59,020
You damn idiot!

432
00:24:16,480 --> 00:24:20,520
But there's a call coming in

433
00:24:21,580 --> 00:24:27,340
With you, I wake up in a good mood

434
00:24:28,020 --> 00:24:31,760
Even boring stories

435
00:24:31,760 --> 00:24:36,560
heat up my whole body

436
00:24:36,560 --> 00:24:43,200
But I want to see my friends

437
00:24:43,200 --> 00:24:58,300
I surely want to be loved, to the point that everyone's a little annoyed,
feeling like we're melting together

438
00:24:58,300 --> 00:25:02,120
I surely want to confide

439
00:25:02,720 --> 00:25:07,960
Somehow, only in love I'm timid

440
00:25:08,480 --> 00:25:15,820
Don't hide everything, not even my bravado

441
00:25:20,400 --> 00:25:23,400
Whoa! You're at it again,
you crazy professor!

442
00:25:23,580 --> 00:25:25,520
This time it's the Air Police Unit!

443
00:25:25,680 --> 00:25:27,600
And what is this airplane anyway!

444
00:25:28,300 --> 00:25:30,140
It's not a homemade-creation contest,
you know

445
00:25:30,140 --> 00:25:32,720
You didn't have to fly in this thing,
did you?

446
00:25:33,300 --> 00:25:35,820
Next time: The Crazy Air Police Unit

447
00:25:36,540 --> 00:25:37,900
I told you I didn't want to, didn't I?

